      "problem": "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨x,{x}^{2}y⟩$ and $f(x,y)=xy,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨y,x⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)=1+{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =xy(1+{x}^{2})+⟨x,{x}^{2}y⟩\\cdot ⟨y,x⟩ \\\\  & =xy+{x}^{3}y+xy+{x}^{3}y \\\\  & =2xy+2{x}^{3}y \\\\  & =2xy(1+{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
